From: Karu KVM integration fixture
Subject: [PATCH] selftests: KVM: require RISC-V timer guest completion

Pinned base: Linux 7.1.2 archive SHA-256
37198c93727be247c9fb5309bb86cd5e496c61e5322cd8c4eca9476bb0b5883f

The RISC-V timer guest emits UCALL_DONE only after all checked iterations.
Unlike the shared host's original policy, do not accept UCALL_SYNC as a pass.
Also verify the guest's interrupt count after copying its shared state back.
The guest body, timer parameters and non-RISC-V host policy are unchanged.

--- a/tools/testing/selftests/kvm/arch_timer.c
+++ b/tools/testing/selftests/kvm/arch_timer.c
@@ -60,8 +60,14 @@ static void *test_vcpu_run(void *arg)
 	pthread_mutex_unlock(&vcpu_done_map_lock);
 
 	switch (get_ucall(vcpu, &uc)) {
+#ifndef __riscv
 	case UCALL_SYNC:
+#endif
 	case UCALL_DONE:
+#ifdef __riscv
+		sync_global_from_guest(vm, *shared_data);
+		TEST_ASSERT_EQ(shared_data->nr_iter, test_args.nr_iter);
+#endif
 		break;
 	case UCALL_ABORT:
 		sync_global_from_guest(vm, *shared_data);
